---
const features = [
  {
    title: 'Enforced Reserve Coverage',
    description:
      'The `RwaToken.sol` contract checks the reserve wallet on every mint and transfer, emitting on-chain events so you can audit solvency in real time.',
    icon: '🛡️'
  },
  {
    title: 'Documented Test Harness',
    description:
      'Foundry-based unit, security, and fuzz tests live in `tests/` to demonstrate the guardrails that keep the alpha implementation honest.',
    icon: '🧪'
  },
  {
    title: 'Known Limitations & Roadmap',
    description:
      'The top-level README lists current gaps—oracle feeds, custody, governance—so contributors can pick up issues and move the project toward readiness.',
    icon: '🧭'
  }
];
---
<section id="features" class="section flex-col gap-16">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
    <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-sm text-primary-200">Why it matters</p>
    <h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold text-white md:text-5xl">All the alpha context in one repo</h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-slate-300">
      The Astro site stays in the new <code>web/</code> workspace, while the Solidity contracts, specs, and tooling remain untouched. Clone the repo to inspect every claim before you ship on top of it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
    {features.map(({ title, description, icon }) => (
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-8" key={title}>
        <div class="mb-4 text-4xl" aria-hidden="true">{icon}</div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">{title}</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300">{description}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
